   "id": "math-0013",
   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "The decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$ is $0.142857142857142857\\ldots$, where the repeating part is $142857$ with a period of $6$.\n\nTo find the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit, we compute $2007 \\mod 6$:\n$$2007 = 6 \\times 334 + 3 = 2004 + 3$$\nSo $2007 \\mod 6 = 3$.\n\nThe $3^{\\text{rd}}$ digit in the repeating block $142857$ is $2$.\n\nTherefore, the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit to the right of the decimal point is $\\boxed{2}$.",
