   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "Using the binomial probability formula, the probability of getting exactly 2 heads in 5 flips of an unfair coin (where heads occurs with probability $\\frac{2}{3}$) is:\n\n$$P(X = 2) = \\binom{5}{2} \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^3 = 10 \\cdot \\frac{4}{9} \\cdot \\frac{1}{27} = \\frac{40}{243}$$\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{40}{243}}$.",
