   "scion_answer": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef digits(n):\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer n, return the product of the odd digits.\n    Return 0 if all digits are even.\n    For example:\n    digits(1)  == 1\n    digits(4)  == 0\n    digits(235) == 15\n    \"\"\"\n    digits_list = [int(d) for d in str(n)]\n    odd_digits = [d for d in digits_list if d % 2 != 0]\n    if not odd_digits:\n        return 0\n    return math.prod(odd_digits)\n```",
